    "raw": "Building a presentation [U1_L5]\n\n    Question   Answer                                                                      Notes\n    1              •   TICK KEYWORDS\n    2              •   To position text, images and graphics on a slide.\n\n    3              •   A common layout that can be applied to on more slides.\n\n    4          Include any three of the following:\n                   • MS PowerPoint\n                   • Open Office Impress\n                   • Google Slides\n                   • Apple Keynote\n\n    5\n                Activity                                                           True            False\n                The order of slides cannot be changed once created.                                 \n                A text box can be freely moved around the slide.                     \n                It is not possible to copy and paste an image into a                                \n                presentation.\n    6              •   A consistent house style will have a similar theme throughout the\n                       presentation.\n\n    7              •   House style = Colour, text and layout choices that are used\n                       consistently throughout a presentation.\n                   •   Target audience = A particular group of people you hope will\n                       enjoy your presentation.\n                   •   User friendly = Easy to navigate with clear information displayed\n                       on screen.\n\n\n    Question   Answer                                              Notes / Marks\n    8_Q1       Insert slides\n    8_Q2       False\n    8_Q3       Sound effect\n    8_Q4       True\n    8_Q5       More animation\n"
