    "raw": "Evaluating a presentation [U1_L8]\n\n    Question   Answer                                                                  Notes\n    1              •   TICK KEYWORDS\n    2              •   To look back at a project when it is complete. Then hopefully\n                       the next project can learn from any mistakes.\n    3          Include any of the following:\n                   • What went well\n                   • What didn’t work so well\n                   • What can be improved\n    4          Include any of the following:\n                   • Smartphones\n                   • Tablets\n                   • Games consoles\n                   • Computer and console games\n                   • Music streaming devices\n    5              • It can be used as a starting point to compare the finished\n                       project to.\n\n    6          Include any of the following:\n                   • Does it meet the brief?\n                   • Will it appeal to the target audience?\n                   • Is the language suitable?\n                   • Are any images and graphics suitable?\n                   • Are there any spelling or grammar mistakes?\n                   • What does the audience think?\n                   • What improvements could be made?\n                   • How could improvements be made?\n    7              • Asking those around you, in your class or home, what they\n                       think of your presentation.\n\n\n\n    Question   Answer                                                                  Notes\n    8_Q1       Network speed\n    8_Q2       Brief\n    8_Q3       Checklist\n    8_Q4       Friends or classmates\n    8_Q5       False\n"
